    "durationMs": 387838,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete. Here's what I built and verified:\n\n**Code** (`src/main.rs`, axum 0.8.4 + sqlx):\n- `POST /links` — parses the body manually (Bytes → serde_json) so malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, and invalid codes all return `422 {\"error\": ...}`; validates url is absolute http/https with a host via the `url` crate and returns the submitted string unchanged; custom codes must be 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`; generated codes are 8 random alphanumerics with collision retry; duplicates return `409`; success returns `201 {\"code\", \"url\", \"clicks\": 0}`.\n- `GET /links/{code}` → `200 {\"code\", \"url\", \"clicks\"}` or `404 {\"error\"}`.\n- `GET /r/{code}` → atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url`, responds `302` with the stored URL as `Location` (verified byte-exact), or `404 {\"error\"}`.\n- `GET /links` → `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` ordered by insertion id ascending.\n- `sqlx::migrate!` applies `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` at startup before binding `0.0.0.0:8000`; connection string comes from `DATABASE_URL` only.\n\n**Ops**: `start.sh` execs the prebuilt release binary in the foreground (builds only if missing, so no network or build at start time); README documents startup.\n\n**Verified**: 36-assertion curl suite covering every requirement (all passing — the two initial \"failures\" were bugs in my test script: curl normalizing `%{redirect_url}` and a stale expected count), persistence across restart (all links, order, and click counts survived, including an increment issued right before the kill), clippy with 0 warnings, and a grader-style `sh start.sh` run on the now-pristine database (migrations applied, empty list, successful create). The server is stopped and test data cleared, ready for the automated suite."
